            "reviewBody": "Excellent Taste - didn't have oatbran, substituted oatmeal - everyone loved it!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "larkspur"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is such a healthy, delicious bread! I converted the recipe to avoid using the bread machine, because I don't have one. Instead, I formed the dough into two long, skinny ropes, cut slashes in the top, and baked them in the oven. The only other change I made was to cut the salt and pepper back to 1/2 tsp. The bread came out very delicious this way...the only other change I would consider is maybe soaking the oat bran in some of the water for 1/2 hour before mixing up the dough so that it would be softer. Thanks so much for sharing...this recipe is a keeper!",
            "datePublished": "2010-01-18T08:30:22.280Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tanaquil"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow---this was phenomenal! I used 2 1/2 cups all purpose flour instead of the other stuff, combined with 1/4 cup of oatmeal. I used fresh, chopped rosemary from our garden. I have been wanting to make this bread for awhile now, and it didn't disappoint---so good! PS Only used about a 1/4 tsp. of black pepper since I was making this for my boys, 1 tsp. pepper seemed a bit much. Also shaped and baked in oven.",
            "datePublished": "2008-06-01T17:02:53.220Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JENIFER13"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I left out the rosemary so I could make mini-burgers using this bread recipe (placed everything in bread machine and pushed 'dough' then rolled into golfball sized balls and baked at 375° for about 12 min.) Kids gobbled them right up!",
            "datePublished": "2007-08-14T13:51:52.250Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "pomplemousse"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very nice. No, this does not rise much, but you have to consider the ingredients here. If you'd like it to rise more, let it rise longer and/or add more vital wheat gluten. The ingredients are pretty heavy in this and they aren't that balanced by the white flour, so bear that in mind. I used all parmesan and dried rosemary. Turned out well. thanks for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2012-08-11T09:33:28.147Z"
          },
          {
